Vulnerability data
------------------
HostCrust Patch Proof reads vulnerability data from OSV.dev (https://osv.dev), which
collects the security data published by Debian, Ubuntu (Canonical), AlmaLinux and
Rocky Linux. Thanks to the OSV.dev team and to each distribution's security team.

This data is not covered by the Apache-2.0 license of the code. It stays under the terms
of each original source; OSV.dev lists them at https://google.github.io/osv.dev/data/
(as of November 2026: Ubuntu CC-BY-SA 4.0, AlmaLinux MIT, Rocky Linux BSD; no license
is stated there for Debian's data). That applies to:

  - tests/fixtures/osv-subset.json.gz: a small extract of OSV.dev bulk data
    (Ubuntu and Debian snapshots of 14 Nov 2026), used by the tests;
  - the prebuilt index (index.sqlite.gz) published with this project's GitHub releases,
    which is derived from OSV.dev bulk data;
  - the sample reports in samples/, which quote that data.

Bulk data downloaded at run time comes directly from OSV.dev
(https://osv-vulnerabilities.storage.googleapis.com) or from the prebuilt index above.
